    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d289">

                <pb facs="0420" n="308" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg308"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 774/763B.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Minister Beaupré.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-07-14"><hi rendition="#italic">July 14,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring to note of November 22, 1909,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d289-f1"/> from the
                    Netherlands minister for foreign affairs, accepting the proposal of the United
                    States for an international opium conference, and suggesting The Hague as the
                    place of meeting, Mr. Wilson says that this proposal is acceptable to the
                    Governments interested and directs Mr. Beaupré to inquire of the minister for
                    foreign affairs if September 15 would be a convenient date for the convening of
                    the conference.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
